WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.344
I C T means information and communication technology.

2
00:00:04.524 --> 00:00:08.220
It is the technology we use to work with information and share it.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.804
Let's follow a message.

4
00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:12.649
You type hello on a keyboard.

5
00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:16.560
Those key presses are input: information entering the computer.

6
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.455
A mouse, microphone, or touchscreen can provide input too.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.343
The C P U runs the app's instructions.

8
00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:27.746
It processes your input so the letters appear on screen.

9
00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:29.627
Think of it as doing the work.

10
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:34.811
While the app is running, RAM holds data it is using right now.

11
00:00:34.991 --> 00:00:36.574
RAM is temporary.

12
00:00:36.754 --> 00:00:39.238
Turn the power off, and its contents are lost.

13
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.611
Save a file, and it goes to persistent storage, such as an S S D.

14
00:00:44.791 --> 00:00:48.447
Unlike RAM, saved files remain when the power is off.

15
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.500
Press send.

16
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.127
A network carries your message as data between devices.

17
00:00:54.307 --> 00:00:59.143
On the other person's screen, the message becomes output: information they can see.

18
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.154
Input brings information in.

19
00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.092
The C P U processes it.

20
00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:06.133
RAM holds working data.

21
00:01:06.313 --> 00:01:08.016
Storage keeps saved files.

22
00:01:08.196 --> 00:01:10.566
Networks let devices share information.

23
00:01:10.746 --> 00:01:11.914
That's I C T.

24
00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:16.405
Quick check: which holds data a program is using right now?

25
00:01:16.585 --> 00:01:17.228
RAM.

26
00:01:17.408 --> 00:01:22.939
Next, open Task Manager and watch C P U, memory, disk, and network activity.
